    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "The policy commits to universal gigabit coverage, which requires significant public subsidy \u2014 \u00a35 billion already committed \u2014 but the spending is on productive infrastructure rather than consumption, meaning long-run fiscal returns are plausible, if unproven from credible independent sources. The 'no property left out' commitment implies further unfunded cost beyond existing programmes.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether the projected economic returns (GDP boost, productivity gains) are large enough and certain enough to offset the additional public cost of connecting the last hardest-to-reach premises, which evidence says is where per-premise costs are highest.",
    "claims": [
